Title: The Lantern Keeper
Credit: sample screenplay for the Fabled Shots demo (original, CC0)

FADE IN:

EXT. HARBOR TOWN - DAWN

Fog rolls over the rooftops. A lone lantern burns at the end of the pier.

MARA (60s, weathered, oilskin coat) walks the length of the pier, checking each lamp.

She stops at the last one. It flickers.

MARA
(quietly)
Not tonight. Not you too.

She picks up a brass key from her belt and opens the lantern housing.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - KITCHEN - MORNING

A small, cluttered room. Charts on the walls. TOMAS (20s, soaked, nervous) sits at the table with a cup of tea he has not touched.

TOMAS
They said the ferry stopped running. Years ago.

MARA
It did.

TOMAS
Then how did I get here?

Mara looks out the window. The fog has not lifted.

MARA
The lamps don't bring boats in. They keep something out.

EXT. CLIFF PATH - NIGHT

Wind. Mara runs along the cliff path, lantern swinging. Behind her, the harbor lights go out one by one.

She falls, catches herself, keeps going.

TOMAS (V.O.)
Mara! The last one!

The pier lantern explodes in a shower of glass.

CUT TO:

EXT. HARBOR TOWN - DAWN (CONTINUOUS)

Silence. The fog is gone. Tomas stands alone on the pier, holding the brass key.

FADE OUT.
